<title>PERU: Peru customs says Jan-May exports up 16.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru customs says Jan-May exports up 16.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's Customs Service said Tuesday exports between January and May were $2.689 billion, up 16.4 percent from the same period last year.</p>
<p>The customs service added in a statement that May exports were $610.5 million, 30.44 percent higher than the same month of 1996.</p>
<p>((-- Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
